{"duration_api_ms":47274,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"0204548c-a824-57b7-bea3-1783011bc81a","total_cost_usd":0.3694494,"usage":{"input_tokens":20,"cache_creation_input_tokens":24311,"cache_read_input_tokens":502907,"output_tokens":3715,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":329},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":24311,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":723,"cache_read_input_tokens":56047,"cache_creation_input_tokens":518,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":518},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":20,"outputTokens":3715,"cacheReadInputTokens":502907,"cacheCreationInputTokens":24311,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3694494,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":329,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":24311,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":10,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I fixed the problem from the rejection: the text-styles cache now turns itself off for good as soon as co-editing is active or a change from another user arrives. The acceptance oracle passes: 6/6 suites, 10066/10323 assertions. As before, `chartEx-serialize` timed out and counts as a pass only because it is recorded as known-broken.\n\n**What changed (`external/sdkjs/common/Drawings/Format/Shape.js`, the only file touched):**\n- The check that runs before the cache is used now also empties and disables it when any of these is true:\n  - `AscCommon.CollaborativeEditing` is missing.\n  - `Is_SingleUser()` is false.\n  - `m_aChanges` holds changes from another user.\n  - Co-authoring is online and the session is not marked single-user.\n- Changes from other users don't add local history points. That is why the old check, which only looked for an empty History, missed them.\n- The rest of the earlier design is unchanged: the cache is used only for placeholders in the presentation editor, only right after opening, and holds at most 5000 entries.\n\n**Decisions:**\n- I chose to switch the cache off rather than add a version counter. It is smaller, stays inside `Shape.js`, and keeps the styles identical as `contract.preserve` requires.\n- The cost: co-edited sessions get no cache hits. So I did not file the version-counter follow-up in `.theseus/spawn/`.\n\n**Not done:** there is still no benchmark on `deck-50.pptx`, so the hit rate and the time saved are unmeasured.\n\nThe Executor log and my friction line are written, and `theseus validate` reports 0 errors and 2 warnings. Both commits are made: one in `external/sdkjs` on `pkt/PKT-0085`, and one for the `.theseus` files in this worktree.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- In co-editing, changes from other users don't create History points. A cache that relies on \"History is empty\" must also check `CollaborativeEditing.Is_SingleUser()` and `m_aChanges`.\n- Styles consumers read through `Get_Pr` copies, so one compiled CStyles object can safely be shared between shapes.","ttft_ms":3452,"type":"result","duration_ms":171090,"uuid":"34aa11dd-2632-415c-8363-ba8cc7cea376","ttft_stream_ms":2375,"time_to_request_ms":559,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":12,"system_prompt":197,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachment